          "description": "Calls the specified tool on the MCP server with arguments"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "MCP Bridge Execution Flow\n├── run() main entry point \u003c-- 1a\n│   ├── mcputil.NewClient() creation \u003c-- skills/mcp_bridge/main.go:110\n│   │   ├── HTTP/SSE transport path \u003c-- 1c\n│   │   └── Stdio transport path \u003c-- 1d\n│   ├── mcputil.Initialize() handshake \u003c-- skills/mcp_bridge/main.go:128\n│   └── mcpClient.CallTool() invocation \u003c-- 1e\n└── parseInput() argument processing \u003c-- skills/mcp_bridge/main.go:152\n    └── Flag vs stdin mode selection \u003c-- skills/mcp_bridge/main.go:154",
      "traceGuide": "# Motivation\n\nThe MCP Bridge solves a critical interoperability problem: **AI coding assistants use different ecosystems but can all speak the Model Context Protocol (MCP)**. Instead of building separate integrations for each assistant (Claude, Codex, OpenCode, etc.), foxctl provides a generic bridge that connects to any MCP server and exposes its tools as native foxctl skills. This creates a **universal adapter** that lets you use MCP tools (like GitHub access, filesystem operations, or web search) from any supported AI assistant with a single implementation.\n\n# Details\n\nThe bridge operates in two modes: **stdio** for local MCP servers and **HTTP/SSE** for remote servers [1c][1d]. When you invoke an MCP tool, the bridge first creates a client with the appropriate transport [1a], performs the MCP initialization handshake to establish the protocol connection, then calls the specific tool with your arguments [1e]. The bridge handles all the protocol details - message formatting, transport management, and error handling - so you can interact with MCP tools using simple JSON input/output. The system also includes an installer that automatically generates foxctl skills from MCP server tool definitions, creating persistent skill wrappers that use the bridge under the hood."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "Provider Configuration Management Operations",
      "description": "Unified system for managing AI coding assistant configurations across Claude, Codex, OpenCode, Factory, and Gemini",
      "locations": [
