          "lineNumber": 177,
          "lineContent": "cmdParts := []string{in.BridgePath}",
          "title": "Bridge command construction",
          "description": "Builds the command that will invoke the MCP bridge for the generated skill"
        },
        {
          "id": "3e",
          "path": "skills/mcp_install/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 276,
          "lineContent": "manifest := map[string]any{",
          "title": "Skill manifest creation",
          "description": "Creates the skill.yaml manifest with MCP tool schema mapped to foxctl signature"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "MCP Skill Installation Flow\n├── run() main entry point \u003c-- 3a\n│   ├── Create MCP client connection \u003c-- skills/mcp_install/main.go:95\n│   │   └── ListTools() discovery \u003c-- 3b\n│   └── For each discovered tool: \u003c-- skills/mcp_install/main.go:142\n│       ├── generateSkill() creation \u003c-- 3c\n│       │   ├── Build bridge command\n│       │   │   └── Add bridge path \u003c-- 3d\n│       │   └── Create skill manifest \u003c-- skills/mcp_install/main.go:276\n│       │       └── Build YAML structure \u003c-- 3e\n│       └── Write skill files to disk \u003c-- skills/mcp_install/main.go:325\n└── Error handling \u0026 logging \u003c-- skills/mcp_install/main.go:145\n    └── Return installed skills list \u003c-- skills/mcp_install/main.go:154",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe MCP installation system solves the **problem of manually creating foxctl skills for every tool on an MCP server**. Instead of writing individual wrapper code for each MCP tool, this system automatically discovers all available tools on an MCP server and generates corresponding foxctl skills. This creates a **universal bridge** between any MCP server and the foxctl ecosystem, enabling users to instantly access all MCP tools as native foxctl skills without manual coding.\n\n## Details\n\nThe system starts by connecting to an MCP server using either stdio or HTTP/SSE transport [3a]. Once connected, it calls `ListTools()` to discover all available tools on the server [3b]. For each discovered tool, it generates a complete foxctl skill by:\n\n1. **Creating a bridge command** that wraps the MCP bridge binary with the correct server connection parameters and tool name [3d]\n2. **Building a skill manifest** that maps the MCP tool's JSON schema to foxctl's parameter format [3e]\n3. **Writing skill files** including the executable wrapper script and YAML manifest to the specified output directory\n\nThe generated skills act as lightweight proxies that forward calls to the original MCP tools through the bridge, maintaining the original tool's functionality while providing native foxctl integration. This approach enables **instant skill generation** for any MCP server without requiring manual wrapper development."
    },
    {
